Bug N/A - preserve native Cairo image formats and normalize big-endian surface bytes on SPARC

On big-endian platforms, Cairo ARGB32/XRGB32 image surfaces are native-endian
ARGB/XRGB byte layouts, while WebRender and most Mozilla image upload paths
expect BGRA/BGRX byte layouts.  The Solaris/SPARC Userland build also keeps the
legacy A8R8G8B8_UINT32 aliases mapped to BGRA/BGRX for WebRender compatibility.

Preserve explicit native Cairo formats where Cairo needs them, and normalize
data crossing back into WebRender, GTK pixbuf, canvas snapshot, and image upload
paths.  This patch is intentionally mostly guarded by the compiler's
__BYTE_ORDER__ condition, with Solaris/SPARC-only guards only around behavior
that depends on the supported Userland runtime path.

Dependency: this is the base format-contract patch for the SPARC rendering
stack. Later Cairo, WebRender, SWGL, shared-image, and BMP/ICO fixes assume the
native-Cairo-versus-WebRender-BGRA/BGRX split established here.

